Z||000000||TWEETIE BIRD||08-05-2001||09:21 PM||||1st Place 84 SE 4 cyl Au nrod<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat1.jpg"> <BR>1st Place 87GT Stock 4-Wheel/Also won Best GM Repaint Stock Color<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat3.jpg"> <BR>1st Place 88 GT Stock Bud & Dee <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat5.jpg"> <BR>ClassAA Custom Coupe 1st Place TWEETIE BIRD<BR>(Fiero Harry's is to the right of me)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat10.jpg"> <BR>All three of the GUYS and their trophies<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat17.jpg"> <BR>If you want to look at any more, here are a few<BR> <A HREF="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat4.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat7.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat7.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat8.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat8.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat9.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat9.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat13.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.avolve.net/users/bhhum/2001Nat13.jpg</A> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||08-05-2001||09:31 PM||||This is the first national event I've missed since joining Fiero owner ranks. Looks like there was a nice setup out there. Sky above you, no rain, lots of Fieros in parking spaces, I should have gone. Were there many parts vendors there? That is one of my favorites about the shows. I will attend next years for sure. Pretty car Tweety, both coupe bodies are my favorite.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TWEETIE BIRD||08-05-2001||09:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>This is the first national event I've missed since joining Fiero owner ranks. Looks like there was a nice setup out there. Sky above you, no rain, lots of Fieros in parking spaces, I should have gone. Were there many parts vendors there? That is one of my favorites about the shows. I will attend next years for sure. Pretty car Tweety, both coupe bodies are my favorite.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It was a beautiful day/days. It was a nice setup but they forgot that when people get fed they also need to use some facilities that were not provided(get my meaning?). That's why we all walked a little funny!LMAO<BR>There were only a couple venders, not like it used to be. All in all we had a great time. <BR>I probably won't be going to the next two unless I get a trailer. Too far for me to drive in this little 2 seater. We made it back today in 9 hours. (550 miles)Wonderful drive, Traffic was bearable.<P>Thanks, I like the coupe style too!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||08-05-2001||10:16 PM||||Yeah, it was a fun time, but little things like no bathroom facilities at the show site put a damper on the weekend.  To be the 17th show, I would have thought things would run smoother.  Even in the show judging - when the awards were announced, it was said that there were no Indy Pace cars there.  The audience had to tell Phil that yes, there was one there and yes, people voted for it.  In Phil's defense, he didn't have anything to do with counting the votes.  He was just reporting what he was told by the people who did.  I guess the same people who counted the Florida election did the car show. <P>I do want to thank Phil for all the hard work he put in.  But even so, a lot fell through the cracks.  ||||reg||6
Z||000004||TWEETIE BIRD||08-05-2001||10:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Yeah, it was a fun time, but little things like no bathroom facilities at the show site put a damper on the weekend.  To be the 17th show, I would have thought things would run smoother.  Even in the show judging - when the awards were announced, it was said that there were no Indy Pace cars there.  The audience had to tell Phil that yes, there was one there and yes, people voted for it.  In Phil's defense, he didn't have anything to do with counting the votes.  He was just reporting what he was told by the people who did.  I guess the same people who counted the Florida election did the car show. <P>I do want to thank Phil for all the hard work he put in.  But even so, a lot fell through the cracks.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yea, It was certainly screwy at the banquet. <BR>They had a lot of people in the wrong classes  at the show too. They did eventually get most everything straightened out. I guess we are all human.<P>That's what makes it interesting and fun, you never know what to expect! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
